  "explanation": "We traverse both linked lists node by node, summing corresponding digits along with any carry from the previous position. We create new nodes for the ones digit of each sum and propagate the carry to the next iteration, effectively simulating column-by-column addition in O(max(N, M)) time.",
  "pseudoCode": "FUNCTION addTwoNumbers(l1, l2):\n    dummy = NEW Node(0), curr = dummy, carry = 0\n    WHILE l1 OR l2 OR carry DO:\n        val1 = l1 ? l1.val : 0\n        val2 = l2 ? l2.val : 0\n        sum = val1 + val2 + carry\n        carry = sum / 10\n        curr.next = NEW Node(sum % 10)\n        curr = curr.next\n        IF l1 THEN l1 = l1.next\n        IF l2 THEN l2 = l2.next\n    END WHILE\n    RETURN dummy.next\nEND FUNCTION",
